 "inter": [],
 "structural_change": "STW-S81c-COLLA 10-22 rg3 PIPELINE (MAIN): IH=1 input relay hops on qi/si (q/s chain +1 edge a reader), KR=1 engine-input relay hops a chunk column (EL+1), per-column kept query-code copies (ql_c had been merged into qh[0] by synthesis: qo[*]->hslice -624 ps x1286 paths). Ports identical; edges priced in MU.S81.CAL (OWNER freeze item 1, STEWARD-S81c ruling 10-22). Prior S81-ELEM2-RG3 10-21 17:30: GPL-0305 fix. Parent kit gates (rg3 514252/514255 @7bd692ad2 pve1; nq db28b4264 ep5) all failed/diverged the same way: std-cell util 2% of placeable (hard 733k um2, std 8k), routability loop never below overflow 0.3 because every routability iteration reverts to a snapshot",
 "why_floorplan": "W band 86.4 (tile W pins qi/si/sid/rst/ck + the walker / landing write logic beside the SRAM W faces); SRAM column x 86.4 (13 high, 20+ um channels, score/metadata queues at the bottom next to the chunk tails, landing in the middle, list / item queue on top); 41-um mid band; 4 abutted hslice chunk columns x 302.4-993.6, y 43.2-1054.1 (slice 0 on top, chain N->S through 25.9-um seams); top channel over the columns = the k_key / ql broadcast + chunk input registers; bottom 43.2 = chunk sums -> tail; E band 43.2 (qo/so/st). N face rqo / rri (1,272 pins, 1.2/um) toward the CTRL-top channel risers.",
